# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Example environment file for Hypothesis → Plan
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) in the project root
# and fill in the values you want to use locally.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Files named `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local` are gitignored
# by default in Vite projects — your key will NOT be committed.
#
# IMPORTANT — VITE_ prefixed variables:
#   * They are BUILD-TIME, BROWSER-SAFE variables.
#   * Vite inlines them into the client bundle at build time.
#   * They are NOT secrets — anyone who loads the site can read them.
#   * Do NOT put truly private keys here. Use a backend proxy for those.
#   * Do NOT add them to Lovable Secrets — Secrets are for server-side
#     runtime only and are not exposed to the browser bundle.
#
# After editing this file you must restart the dev server so Vite
# picks up the new values.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional — Semantic Scholar API key.
# Used by src/lib/services.ts → searchLiterature() to send the
# `x-api-key` header for higher rate limits.
#
# If this variable is missing, empty, or the live request fails
# (429, 403, CORS, network error, empty results), the app
# automatically falls back to verified source-backed seed data.
# Live Semantic Scholar search is manual-only — triggered by the
# "Refresh from Semantic Scholar" button on the project page.
#
# Get a key: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key
VITE_SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=s2k-Pi8GmgTz7Dxn3C9xwPxSw2PhBZbTMn4M5wzzjcch
